That's along the same lines as I was thinking. I was imagining some kind
of tool that would do various statistical analysis (e.g. frequency of
creatures and objects) and put aggregate data up on a web page (perhaps
delayed until after the bones were gone or the saved game had ended,
to avoid leaking information players could use to advantage in a specific
game).

I can also imagine hacks which would, e.g., "decay" sitting bones files
over days or weeks of wall time. Maybe a Colossal-Cave-style thief who'd
wander through, grab the better loot, and haul it back to his lair deep
within the mazes. 

> What I had been advocating was: not to introduce a format that would
